    <!-- COVER BANNER -->
    <div class="cover-banner">
      <h1>EXAM DUTY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM</h1>
      <p>Deployment &bull; System Architecture &bull; Technical Report</p>
    </div>

    <table class="meta-table">
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Prepared By:</strong> Chandana IT Solutions</td>
        <td><strong>Prepared For:</strong> Chandana Sub Group / Operations</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Date:</strong> October 2026</td>
        <td><strong>Version:</strong> 2.2 (Enterprise Handover Edition)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Repository:</strong> github.com/mayurChandanaitso/trackClockExam</td>
        <td><strong>Platform Stack:</strong> React 18 (Vite), NestJS 11, TypeORM, PostgreSQL/MySQL</td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <!-- 1. OVERVIEW -->
    <h2>1. Overview</h2>
    <p>
      The <strong>Exam Duty Management System (TrackClock)</strong> is a centralized web and mobile platform designed for assigning, monitoring, and validating examination personnel across multi-city testing networks. It replaces manual paperwork with a digital, conflict-free scheduling engine, digital attendance photo-proof verification, and dynamic month-wise analytical reporting.
    </p>
    <p>The system comprises two core components:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Frontend Web Application:</strong> A responsive React 18 (Vite) client providing an <em>Admin Management Portal</em> for operations managers and a mobile-optimized <em>Staff Web Portal</em> for invigilators and center staff.</li>
      <li><strong>Backend REST API:</strong> A NestJS 11 (Node.js 22) application gateway providing role-based security, conflict-free scheduling algorithms, synchronous Multer attendance proof ingestion, and normalized relational persistence.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- 2. ARCHITECTURE -->
    <h2>2. Architecture</h2>
    <p>
      Users interact with the frontend through any standard web or mobile browser. The client communicates via encrypted HTTPS REST requests to the NestJS backend API gateway, which interacts with the relational database through TypeORM with full foreign key constraints and connection pooling.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Layer</th>
          <th>Technology</th>
          <th>Hosting Specification</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Frontend</strong></td><td>React 18, TypeScript, Vite 6</td><td>Node.js Web App / Managed Cloud CDN</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Backend API</strong></td><td>NestJS 11, TypeORM 0.3, Node.js 22</td><td>Node.js Web App Gateway with PM2</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Database</strong></td><td>PostgreSQL / MySQL (Managed)</td><td>Managed Relational Cloud Database (8 Normalized Tables)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>File Storage</strong></td><td>Local Encrypted Storage / Cloud Bucket</td><td>Uploaded attendance proof images and PDF room documents</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>SSL / HTTPS</strong></td><td>TLS 1.3 Encryption</td><td>Automated SSL Certificates</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div style="text-align:center; margin:16px 0 24px 0;">
    <img src="figure_2_1_architecture.png" alt="Figure 2.1: Multi-Tier System Component Architecture" style="max-width:100%; height:auto; border:1px solid #CBD5E1; border-radius:6px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);" />
    <div style="font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; color:#1E3A8A; margin-top:6px;">Figure 2.1: Multi-Tier System Component Architecture</div>
  </div>

