    <!-- 4. HOSTING SETUP -->
    <h2>4. Hosting Setup</h2>
    <p>
      The application runs as optimized Node.js Web Apps deployed directly from the GitHub version control repository. Each push or release to the main branch is built and deployed automatically.
    </p>

    <h3>4.1 Backend Web App Configuration</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Setting Name</th><th>Configured Value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Source Repository</td><td>GitHub repository (branch <code>main</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Framework Preset</td><td>NestJS / Node.js</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Node.js Runtime Version</td><td>22.x</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Root Directory</td><td><code>ExamDutyManagement/backend</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Package Manager</td><td>npm</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Build Command</td><td><code>npm run build</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Output Directory</td><td><code>dist</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Application Entry File</td><td><code>dist/main.js</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>4.2 Frontend Web App Configuration</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Setting Name</th><th>Configured Value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Source Repository</td><td>GitHub repository (branch <code>main</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Framework Preset</td><td>Vite / React</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Node.js Runtime Version</td><td>22.x</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Root Directory</td><td><code>ExamDutyManagement/frontend</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Package Manager</td><td>npm</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Build Command</td><td><code>npm run build</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Output Directory</td><td><code>dist</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Entry File</td><td><code>index.html</code> (SPA Rewrites enabled)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- 5. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES -->
    <h2>5. Environment Variables Configuration</h2>
    <p>
      Application configuration settings are isolated into environment variables configured on the hosting server. Credentials must never be committed to public repositories.
    </p>

    <h3>5.1 Backend Environment Variables</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Purpose &amp; Description</th><th>Example / Production Setting</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>PORT</code></td><td>API Gateway port</td><td><code>3000</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DB_HOST</code></td><td>Database server address</td><td><code>localhost</code> / Managed DB Host</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DB_PORT</code></td><td>Database connection port</td><td><code>5432</code> (PostgreSQL) / <code>3306</code> (MySQL)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DB_DATABASE</code> / <code>DB_NAME</code></td><td>Database instance name</td><td><code>examduty_production_db</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DB_USERNAME</code> / <code>DB_USER</code></td><td>Database user account</td><td><code>examduty_user</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DB_PASSWORD</code></td><td>Database authentication password</td><td>Cryptographic Secret (Rotated)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DB_SSL</code></td><td>Enforce TLS database traffic</td><td><code>true</code> in production</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DB_SYNCHRONIZE</code></td><td>Auto-create database tables</td><td><code>false</code> in production (Migrations used)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>JWT_SECRET</code></td><td>Signing key for JWT tokens</td><td>Cryptographic Secret</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CORS_ORIGIN</code></td><td>Permitted frontend origin</td><td><code>https://trackclockexam.chandanaitsolutions.com</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>5.2 Frontend Environment Variables</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Purpose &amp; Description</th><th>Example / Production Setting</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>VITE_API_URL</code></td><td>Base backend API gateway endpoint</td><td><code>https://api-trackclockexam.chandanaitsolutions.com/api</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>VITE_APP_TITLE</code></td><td>Application page title</td><td><code>Exam Duty Management System</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- 6. DATABASE & DATA DICTIONARY -->
    <h2>6. Database Architecture &amp; Data Dictionary</h2>
    <p>
      The persistence tier consists of 8 normalized relational tables configured with strict foreign key integrity, cascade delete protection, and unique constraints:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Table Name</th>
          <th>Primary Key</th>
          <th>Foreign Keys</th>
          <th>Core Attributes &amp; Constraints</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>duties</code></td><td><code>id</code> (UUID)</td><td><code>employeeId</code>, <code>centerId</code>, <code>cityId</code>, <code>examId</code>, <code>roleId</code>, <code>shiftId</code>, <code>attendanceFileId</code></td><td><code>dutyDate</code> (VARCHAR), <code>dutyType</code> ('Exam'|'Mock'), <code>status</code> ('Pending'|'Approved'|'Rejected'), <code>reportingTime</code>, <code>shiftEndTime</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>employees</code></td><td><code>id</code> (UUID)</td><td>None</td><td><code>resourceId</code> (Unique VARCHAR), <code>name</code>, <code>mobile</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>aadhaarNumber</code>, <code>panNumber</code>, <code>city</code>, <code>isActive</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>exams</code></td><td><code>id</code> (UUID)</td><td>None</td><td><code>code</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>type</code> ('Exam'|'Mock'), <code>description</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>centers</code></td><td><code>id</code> (UUID)</td><td><code>cityId</code> &rarr; <code>cities(id)</code></td><td><code>centerCode</code>, <code>centerName</code>, <code>address</code>, <code>contactPerson</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>cities</code></td><td><code>id</code> (UUID)</td><td>None</td><td><code>name</code> (Unique: Mysore, Bangalore, Hassan, Mandya, etc.), <code>state</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>roles</code></td><td><code>id</code> (UUID)</td><td>None</td><td><code>code</code> (Invigilator, Center Supt, Tech Support), <code>title</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>shifts</code></td><td><code>id</code> (UUID)</td><td>None</td><td><code>name</code> ('Shift 1', 'Shift 2'), <code>startTime</code>, <code>endTime</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>attendance_files</code></td><td><code>id</code> (UUID)</td><td>Referenced by <code>duties</code></td><td><code>originalName</code>, <code>filePath</code>, <code>mimeType</code>, <code>size</code>, <code>createdAt</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div style="text-align:center; margin:16px 0 24px 0;">
    <img src="figure_6_1_er_diagram.png" alt="Figure 6.1: Entity-Relationship (ER) Relational Schema Model" style="max-width:100%; height:auto; border:1px solid #CBD5E1; border-radius:6px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);" />
    <div style="font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; color:#1E3A8A; margin-top:6px;">Figure 6.1: Entity-Relationship (ER) Relational Schema Model</div>
  </div>

    <!-- 7. SYSTEM FLOW -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>7. End-to-End System Flow</h2>
    <p>
      The application coordinates workforce assignments across four deterministic stages:
    </p>
    <div style="text-align:center; margin:16px 0 24px 0;">
    <img src="figure_7_1_system_flow.png" alt="Figure 7.1: Continuous Operational System Flow" style="max-width:100%; height:auto; border:1px solid #CBD5E1; border-radius:6px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);" />
    <div style="font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; color:#1E3A8A; margin-top:6px;">Figure 7.1: Continuous Operational System Flow</div>
  </div>

    <ol>
      <li><strong>Master Setup &amp; Employee Onboarding:</strong> Operations administrators populate baseline institutional data (cities, examination centers, exam rosters) and register personnel using verified Resource IDs. Real-time sequence validation prevents dummy test inputs. Upon saving, a floating SweetAlert toast confirms success.</li>
      <li><strong>Duty Allocation &amp; Conflict Engine:</strong> Administrators assign duties selecting explicitly between <strong>Exam</strong> and <strong>Mock</strong> sessions. The scheduling engine validates employee availability, preventing duplicate bookings for the same personnel on matching dates and shifts.</li>
      <li><strong>Staff Attendance Submission:</strong> On testing day, field personnel sign into the mobile portal, review their assigned shifts under <strong>Mark Duties</strong>, and capture real-time photo proof or counter-signed room sheets. The Multer guard verifies file MIME types synchronously.</li>
      <li><strong>Dynamic Real-Time Analytics:</strong> System metrics aggregate instantly without page refreshes: Total Duties, This Month duties, Exam duties, and Mock duties, tracked continuously across a monthly histogram bar chart.</li>
    </ol>

    <!-- 8. PORTAL FUNCTIONALITY WALKTHROUGH -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>8. Detailed Portal Walkthrough &amp; Functional Modules</h2>
    <p>
      The application architecture provides tailored user experiences for both administrators and field workforce members:
    </p>

    <div style="text-align:center; margin:16px 0 24px 0;">
    <img src="figure_8_1_portal_navigation.png" alt="Figure 8.1: Portal Functional Architecture & Module Map" style="max-width:100%; height:auto; border:1px solid #CBD5E1; border-radius:6px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);" />
    <div style="font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; color:#1E3A8A; margin-top:6px;">Figure 8.1: Portal Functional Architecture & Module Map</div>
  </div>

    <h3>8.1 Admin Management Portal Modules</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Dashboard:</strong> Executive monitoring center featuring 4 live KPI cards (<em>TOTAL DUTIES</em>, <em>THIS MONTH</em>, <em>EXAMS</em>, and <em>MOCKS</em>) alongside an interactive monthly duty overview bar chart (April through October) and the live <strong>Mark Duties</strong> feed.</li>
      <li><strong>Add Employee (Workforce Management):</strong> Single-entry staff registration enforcing Resource ID uniqueness, mobile verification, Aadhaar/PAN validation, and multi-city selection. Includes bulk Excel workforce ingestion and a paginated workforce directory. Clicking <em>Save &amp; Register Employee</em> triggers the SweetAlert toast notification: <code>(✓) Employee "[Name]" registered successfully.</code></li>
      <li><strong>Add City (Location Master):</strong> Management screen to register testing cities and administrative jurisdictions across Karnataka (Mysore, Bangalore, Hassan, Mandya, etc.).</li>
      <li><strong>Add Exam Name (Examination Master):</strong> Register examination sessions, defining exam code, descriptive title, and classifying whether the session is an official <strong>Exam</strong> or a preparatory <strong>Mock Test</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Add Exam Center Name (Venue Master):</strong> Register physical venues and testing institutions, linking venue address, center superintendent contacts, and geographic city assignment.</li>
      <li><strong>Assign Duties to Employee (Duty Scheduling):</strong> Allocation module allowing administrators to link an employee to an exam, date, center venue, role, and shift. Features a prominent toggle between <strong>Exam</strong> and <strong>Mock</strong> duty types and auto-populates reporting times. The conflict engine prevents overlapping assignments.</li>
      <li><strong>Admin Profile:</strong> Governance view managing administrative access credentials, session status, and security audit logs.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>8.2 Employee / Staff Mobile Portal Modules</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Staff Authentication:</strong> Streamlined authentication requiring only the employee's unique Resource ID and registered Mobile Number / PIN.</li>
      <li><strong>Staff Dashboard:</strong> Mobile-optimized overview displaying personal cumulative duties completed, current month quota, and assigned shifts.</li>
      <li><strong>"Mark Duties" Feed:</strong> Clean list of all assigned upcoming and current duties detailing exam name, duty date, center venue, assigned role, and shift timing.</li>
      <li><strong>Attendance Proof Submission:</strong> One-tap camera viewfinder integration allowing staff to capture live on-site attendance photos or upload counter-signed room invigilation sheets. Synchronous validation prevents process timeouts. Submitting attendance triggers the top-floating toast notification: <code>(✓) Attendance submitted successfully.</code></li>
      <li><strong>Duty Status Tracking:</strong> Real-time status indicators (<code>Pending</code>, <code>Approved</code>, or <code>Rejected</code>) ensuring staff have continuous visibility into duty verification.</li>
      <li><strong>Staff Profile:</strong> Personal view displaying registered contact details, assigned operational cities, and KYC verification records.</li>
    </ol>

    <!-- 9. COMPLETE SYSTEM DIAGRAMS -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>9. Complete System &amp; UML Diagrams</h2>
    <p>
