  </div>

    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h3>9.4 Data Flow Diagrams (DFD Level 0 &amp; Level 1)</h3>
    <p>
      Decomposes data flow across external entities, processing modules, and database data stores:
    </p>
    <div style="text-align:center; margin:16px 0 24px 0;">
    <img src="figure_9_4_data_flow_diagram.png" alt="Figure 9.4: Data Flow Diagram (DFD Level 0 & Level 1 Decomposition)" style="max-width:100%; height:auto; border:1px solid #CBD5E1; border-radius:6px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);" />
    <div style="font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; color:#1E3A8A; margin-top:6px;">Figure 9.4: Data Flow Diagram (DFD Level 0 & Level 1 Decomposition)</div>
  </div>

    <!-- 10. CODEBASE FOLDER STRUCTURE & CONFIG -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>10. Codebase Directory Structure &amp; Configurations</h2>
    <p>
      The repository maintains a clean separation between backend micro-services, frontend views, and deployment configurations:
    </p>
    <div class="code-box">ExamDutyManagement/
├── backend/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── config/database.config.ts    # Database connection & connection pool settings
│   │   ├── entities/                    # 8 TypeORM entity schema models
│   │   ├── modules/
│   │   │   ├── attendance/              # Multer proof file stream handler
│   │   │   ├── auth/                    # Dual authentication & JWT guard
│   │   │   ├── dashboard/               # Metric aggregation & monthly calculations
│   │   │   ├── duties/                  # Duty CRUD & conflict detection engine
│   │   │   ├── master-data/             # Cities, Centers, Exams, Roles, Shifts
│   │   │   └── seed/                    # Baseline dataset seeder
│   │   ├── health/                      # Healthcheck probe controller
│   │   ├── app.module.ts                # Root application dependency container
│   │   └── main.ts                      # Bootstrap & CORS configuration
│   ├── package.json                     # Backend dependencies & build scripts
│   └── tsconfig.json                    # Backend TypeScript compiler configuration
├── frontend/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/
│   │   │   ├── MonthlyChart.tsx         # Monthly Exam vs. Mock bar chart
│   │   │   ├── RecentDutiesTable.tsx    # "Mark Duties" feed table component
│   │   │   ├── SearchableSelect.tsx     # Auto-complete select with dynamic font clamp
│   │   │   ├── StatCard.tsx             # 4-card metric KPI widget
│   │   │   └── SweetAlertToast.tsx      # Floating SweetAlert toast notification
│   │   ├── pages/                       # Screen views (AddDuty, AddEmployee, Dashboard)
│   │   ├── styles/App.css               # Corporate design tokens & styling
│   │   └── vite.config.ts               # Bundler settings & vendor chunk isolation
└── documentation/                       # Technical reports (.html, .doc, .docx, .pdf)</div>

    <h3>10.1 Key Configuration Files</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong><code>database.config.ts</code>:</strong> Enforces connection pooling (<code>max: 20</code>, <code>idleTimeout: 30000ms</code>), SSL certificate validation, and disables destructive auto-synchronization in production.</li>
      <li><strong><code>vite.config.ts</code>:</strong> Implements Rollup manual chunking to separate large vendor libraries (React, React Router) and spreadsheet processing (XLSX) into distinct cached assets.</li>
      <li><strong><code>tsconfig.json</code>:</strong> Configured with strict type checking, decorator metadata enabled for TypeORM entities, and ES2022 target output.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- 11. DEPLOYMENT PROCEDURE -->
    <h2>11. Deployment Procedure (Summary)</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Subdomains:</strong> Create the frontend and backend subdomains in the hosting control panel (e.g. <code>trackclockexam.chandanaitsolutions.com</code> and <code>api-trackclockexam.chandanaitsolutions.com</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>Database Provisioning:</strong> Create the relational database and user account in the hosting database manager, then import the database schema.</li>
      <li><strong>Backend Web App Deployment:</strong> Create a Node.js Web App linked to the GitHub repository using the settings in Section 4.1 and the environment variables in Section 5.1. Trigger deployment build.</li>
      <li><strong>Verify Backend:</strong> Open the health check URL (<code>/api/health</code>) and confirm <code>{"status":"ok","database":"connected"}</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Frontend Web App Deployment:</strong> Create the frontend Web App using the settings in Section 4.2 and the build variable <code>VITE_API_URL</code>. Deploy.</li>
      <li><strong>Verify Portal:</strong> Access the application domain over HTTPS and verify administrative and staff authentication.</li>
    </ol>

    <!-- 12. UPDATING APPLICATION -->
    <h2>12. Updating the Application</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Commit and push verified changes to the <code>main</code> branch on GitHub.</li>
      <li>In the hosting panel, navigate to the relevant Web App (backend, frontend, or both) and trigger <strong>Redeploy</strong>.</li>
      <li>Monitor the build log until deployment status indicates <code>Completed</code>.</li>
      <li>Verify the health check endpoint and test portal login.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Fail-Safe Rollback:</strong> If a deployment fails, the previous working version remains active automatically. Review the build log, resolve the error, and re-trigger deployment.
    </div>

    <!-- 13. ACCESS AND CREDENTIALS -->
    <h2>13. Access and Credentials Matrix</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>User Role</th>
          <th>Portal Interface</th>
          <th>Login Identifier</th>
          <th>Default Password / PIN</th>
          <th>Access Privileges</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Super Administrator</strong></td><td>Desktop Management Portal</td><td><code>admin</code> or <code>17655</code></td><td><code>admin123</code></td><td>Full governance: Staff KYC, duty scheduling (Exam/Mock), attendance audits, Excel exports.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Operations Manager</strong></td><td>Desktop Management Portal</td><td><code>mohan</code></td><td><code>admin123</code></td><td>Center coordination, duty allocation, attendance sheet reviews.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Staff Invigilator</strong></td><td>Mobile Web PWA</td><td>Resource ID (e.g. <code>23625</code>)</td><td>Registered Mobile PIN</td><td>Mobile view: "Mark Duties" feed, photo proof submission, monthly quota tracking.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- 14. SECURITY RECOMMENDATIONS -->
    <h2>14. Security Hardening &amp; Enhancements (v2.2)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Multer CVE-2025-47279 Remediation:</strong> Upgraded to <code>multer@2.5.0</code> and enforced synchronous <code>fileFilter</code> functions across all upload routes. This eliminates stream abort unhandled errors and completely prevents backend process crashes.</li>
      <li><strong>SweetAlert Toast Notification Standard:</strong> Replaced disruptive modal dialogs with clean, floating top-center toast notifications featuring an emerald checkmark badge (<code>(✓)</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>Anti-Sequence Input Protection:</strong> Enforced client-side and server-side sequence checks that reject continuous dummy sequences (e.g. <code>123456</code>) in mobile and Aadhaar fields.</li>
      <li><strong>Neutral Form Initialization:</strong> Duty date, city, center, exam, role, shift, and employee are unselected by default, preventing unintentional duplicate submissions.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- 15. BACKUPS AND MAINTENANCE -->
    <h2>15. Backups and Maintenance</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Database Backups:</strong> Enable automated daily snapshots on the hosting database manager and export an offline SQL dump prior to major application version updates.</li>
      <li><strong>Uploaded Document Storage:</strong> Attendance proof images and room sheets are stored in the persistent uploads directory. Ensure this directory is linked to persistent block storage to survive container redeployments.</li>
      <li><strong>Uptime Monitoring:</strong> Configure automated uptime monitoring on the <code>/api/health</code> endpoint to notify administrators immediately in the event of database connectivity drops.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- 16. TROUBLESHOOTING MATRIX -->
    <h2>16. Troubleshooting Matrix</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Symptom</th>
          <th>Likely Cause</th>
          <th>Corrective Action</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Health check shows database error</td><td>Wrong database name, host, or credentials</td><td>Verify environment variables in Section 5.1 and confirm database server is reachable.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Build fails with <code>command not found</code></td><td>Missing dependencies or wrong node version</td><td>Ensure Node.js 22.x is selected and package dependencies are installed via <code>npm install</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Login displays network error</td><td><code>VITE_API_URL</code> missing or incorrect at build time</td><td>Set the correct backend URL in frontend environment variables and redeploy the frontend.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Portal opens but displays empty tables</td><td>CORS origin misconfiguration</td><td>Confirm <code>CORS_ORIGIN</code> on backend includes the exact frontend domain without trailing slashes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Page reload returns HTTP 404</td><td>SPA rewrite rule missing</td><td>Ensure single-page routing rewrite rules (<code>index.html</code>) are enabled in hosting configuration.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- 17. HANDOVER CHECKLIST -->
    <h2>17. Operational Handover Checklist</h2>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Frontend and backend subdomains operational and secured over HTTPS (TLS 1.3).</li>
      <li>Backend REST API returning <code>database: connected</code> on healthcheck probe.</li>
      <li>Super Admin, Operations Manager, and Staff logins verified.</li>
      <li>SweetAlert toast notifications operational across employee registration and attendance upload.</li>
      <li>Dynamic Exam vs. Mock counting active across summary cards and monthly histogram charts.</li>
      <li>Database credentials excluded from version control and secured on hosting server.</li>
      <li>Full project technical documentation delivered in HTML, Microsoft Word (.doc), and True PDF formats.</li>
    </ul>

    <div style="margin-top: 35pt; border-top: 1pt solid #CBD5E1; padding-top: 12pt; font-size: 9pt; color: #64748B; display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
